{%- comment -%}
  Renders Google reviews synced into metaobjects by the sync-google-reviews Claude skill.

  The cards come from snippets/mionas-google-review-card.liquid -- the same snippet the hand-configured
  blocks/mionas-review-card.liquid renders -- so a Google review and a hand-entered testimonial are
  the same component with different data behind them.

  Why a section and not a block: a *merchant-added* block is one card, and the carousel treats each
  such block as one slide, so a block that looped would put every review inside a single slide. A
  section can own both the row and the summary line beneath it, which is also why no separate
  container section is needed to place the summary. The card is still a block -- see below -- just a
  static one the section renders itself, which is a different thing.

  The card and the summary are *static* blocks -- rendered with content_for 'block' plus an explicit
  type and id -- the same mechanism sections/mionas-split-panel.liquid uses for its two sides and
  sections/product-list.liquid for its header and its cards. A static slot cannot be removed,
  reordered or duplicated, so the section always has exactly one card design and exactly one summary
  row, while everything inside them is the merchant's to configure. That is why this file carries no
  `heading`, `horizontal_alignment`, `profile_url`, `reviews_label`, `link_label` or `card_*`
  settings: each of those now belongs to the block that renders it.

  The card slot sits inside the selection loop below, rendered once per chosen review with the
  review's fields passed as parameters on the tag. content_for 'block' accepts arbitrary parameters
  and static blocks may be rendered in a for-loop; because every iteration shares the id
  'static-review-card', the theme editor shows a single card block whose settings govern every card
  -- the same behaviour product-list gets from _product-card. See
  blocks/_mionas-google-review-card.liquid for why parameters rather than
  closest.metaobject.google_review.

  The summary slot is a container (blocks/_mionas-google-reviews-summary.liquid) rendering through
  snippets/group.liquid, so its four parts -- score, separator, count, link -- are separate child
  blocks the merchant can restyle, reorder, remove or add to. It could not be a native `group`
  because a native group whitelists `@theme`, which covers public theme blocks only, and the score
  and count must be private: they read metaobjects.google_review_summary and would render a summary
  of nothing anywhere else.

  There is no built-in heading. Instead the section opens a free content_for 'blocks' region above
  the cards, so a heading is whatever block the merchant chooses to put there -- a Mionas: Text, an
  image, a button -- rather than a baked-in text setting that duplicates what mionas-text already
  does better.

  Layout is merchant-controlled the same way sections/product-list.liquid does it: every selected
  card is captured into one string separated by <!--@list/split-->, that string is split into an
  array, and both are handed to snippets/resource-list.liquid, which owns grid / carousel /
  editorial rendering and the mobile-carousel fallback. This section is data-driven (it loops
  metaobjects, not merchant-authored blocks) exactly like product-list is, so the same capture-and-
  split indirection is what buys layout settings without turning each review into a merchant-added
  block.

  Why day-of-year rotation and not random: Shopify full-page-caches storefront pages for anonymous
  visitors and Liquid has no random filter, so a per-request pick would be frozen into cached HTML
  and served identically to everyone anyway. Seeding from the day rotates the selection daily, stays
  cache-friendly, needs no JavaScript, and leaves the reviews visible to search engines.

  Why a stride instead of a contiguous window: picking offset, offset+1, offset+2, ... always shows
  entries adjacent in creation order, so on any given day the cards look clustered from a similar
  period rather than sampled from the whole pool. Picking every Nth entry instead (offset + i*stride)
  spreads the selection across the full enabled pool. For every pick to land on a distinct entry,
  stride must be coprime with enabled_count -- if it shares a common factor, the sequence of picks
  cycles back on itself before reaching show_count distinct values and the same review renders twice.
  enabled_count varies at runtime (reviews get added/disabled), so the stride is computed below rather
  than hardcoded: start near enabled_count / show_count (spreads picks evenly across the pool) and
  walk forward until a coprime value is found, via a bounded Euclidean-algorithm gcd check, falling
  back to 1 (a plain contiguous window) if nothing else qualifies.

  Never bracket-index the pool with a variable: pool[0] works in Liquid but pool[i] silently returns
  nil, which once shipped here as cards with no quote, no name and five filled stars. Selection is
  therefore always a {% raw %}{% for %}{% endraw %} walk with a membership test per entry.

  metaobjects.<type>.values loops a maximum of 50 entries, oldest-created-first -- this is Shopify
  Liquid's platform ceiling and cannot be changed. The sync skill's transform.jq caps each RUN at 25
  reviews, a separate and much smaller curation cap chosen to leave headroom below the 50-entry
  ceiling; that per-run cap is not cumulative -- the skill is create-only and never trims, so stored
  entries accumulate across runs and anything past slot 50 (the platform ceiling) is invisible here.
  Keeping the total at 50 or fewer is an operator task done in the Shopify admin, not something this
  section or the skill enforces. Switching a review's enabled field off does NOT free a slot: the
  filter below runs after Liquid has already truncated to 50. See the "Housekeeping" section of
  .claude/skills/sync-google-reviews/SKILL.md.

  Display order is metaobject creation order, NOT newest-first. Entries carry created_at, but nothing
  sorts on it -- deliberately. Liquid cannot sort out of the 50-entry truncation, which happens before
  any sort or filter could run, so sorting here would reorder an already-wrong window. The rotation
  below therefore walks entries in creation order.

  No structured data is emitted here on purpose: Google's structured-data policy excludes
  self-serving aggregate ratings gathered from another platform.

  Every colour comes from existing --review-card-* and --link-* tokens; this section introduces no
  new token and touches neither assets/design-tokens.css nor ../design-system.
{%- endcomment -%}

{% liquid
  assign pool = metaobjects.google_review.values

  # A review with no enabled value predates the field and is treated as enabled, so entries
  # created before this field existed keep rendering.
  assign enabled_count = 0
  for review in pool
    if review.enabled.value == false
      continue
    endif
    assign enabled_count = enabled_count | plus: 1
  endfor
%}

{%- comment -%}
  Everything the section emits lives inside this guard: with no enabled entries there is no grid, no
  heading, no summary, no background element and no resource-list wrapper -- and the modulo below is
  never reached with a zero divisor.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- if enabled_count > 0 -%}
  {%- liquid
    if section.settings.background_color != blank
      render 'contrast-override', background_color: section.settings.background_color, section_id: section.id
    endif

    assign day_of_year = 'now' | date: '%j' | plus: 0
    assign offset = day_of_year | modulo: enabled_count
    assign show_count = section.settings.review_count
    if enabled_count < show_count
      assign show_count = enabled_count
    endif

    # Approximate stride: spread show_count picks evenly across enabled_count entries. Force
    # float division (divided_by truncates when both operands are integers) and round to the
    # nearest whole stride -- truncating instead would bias small pools toward stride 1, which
    # is just the old contiguous window in disguise.
    assign stride = enabled_count | times: 1.0 | divided_by: show_count | round
    if stride < 1
      assign stride = 1
    endif

    # Walk forward from the approximate stride until gcd(candidate, enabled_count) == 1.
    # The (0..enabled_count) range covers every residue mod enabled_count at least once, so a
    # coprime candidate is always found when enabled_count > 1 (candidate == 1 is always coprime).
    assign found_stride = 0
    for i in (0..enabled_count)
      assign candidate = stride | plus: i
      assign candidate = candidate | modulo: enabled_count
      # candidate 0 is never coprime with enabled_count (unless enabled_count is 1, handled by
      # the fallback below), so skip it rather than let a false gcd of enabled_count through.
      if candidate == 0
        continue
      endif

      assign gcd_a = candidate
      assign gcd_b = enabled_count
      for j in (0..enabled_count)
        if gcd_b == 0
          break
        endif
        assign gcd_remainder = gcd_a | modulo: gcd_b
        assign gcd_a = gcd_b
        assign gcd_b = gcd_remainder
      endfor

      if gcd_a == 1
        assign found_stride = candidate
        break
      endif
    endfor

    if found_stride == 0
      assign found_stride = 1
    endif
    assign stride = found_stride

    assign show_count_minus_1 = show_count | minus: 1
  -%}

  <div
    class="section-background{% if section.settings.background_color != blank %} color-custom-{{ section.id }}{% endif %}"
  ></div>
  <div
    class="
      mionas-google-reviews
      section
      section--{{ section.settings.section_width }}
      {% if section.settings.background_color != blank %}color-custom-{{ section.id }}{% endif %}
      section-resource-list
      spacing-style
      gap-style
    "
    style="
      {% render 'spacing-style', settings: section.settings %}
      {% render 'gap-style', value: section.settings.gap %}
    "
  >
    {%- comment -%}
      The free region: whatever the merchant wants above the cards -- a Mionas: Text heading, an
      image, a button, an app block. A section may declare only ONE content_for 'blocks' area, so
      its position is a real choice, and above is the more useful end here: the summary row already
      sits below the cards and is itself a group that accepts @theme/@app children, so blocks can
      still be added underneath by dropping them into it.

      Whitespace control on the tag is load-bearing: base.css hides
      .section-resource-list__content:empty, and a stray newline inside the div would be a text node
      that defeats :empty, leaving a --gap-sized hole above the cards when no block is added.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <div class="section-resource-list__content">{%- content_for 'blocks' -%}</div>

    {%- comment -%}
      Capture the selected cards into one string, separated the way product-list separates its
      product cards. The separator is emitted BEFORE every card after the first rather than after
      every card but the last: forloop.last refers to the whole pool here, not to the subset that
      passes the selection test, so a rendered-counter is the only correct marker.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- capture list_items -%}
      {%- assign enabled_index = -1 -%}
      {%- assign rendered_count = 0 -%}
      {%- for review in pool -%}
        {%- if review.enabled.value == false -%}
          {%- continue -%}
        {%- endif -%}
        {%- assign enabled_index = enabled_index | plus: 1 -%}
        {%- liquid
          assign selected = false
          for i in (0..show_count_minus_1)
            assign pick = i | times: stride
            assign pick = pick | plus: offset
            assign pick = pick | modulo: enabled_count
            if pick == enabled_index
              assign selected = true
              break
            endif
          endfor
        -%}
        {%- if selected -%}
          {%- if rendered_count > 0 -%}<!--@list/split-->{%- endif -%}
          <div class="resource-list__item">
            {% comment %}
              card_index is passed only so the block can build a unique accessible name for its
              "Leer más" trigger when the reviewer's name is hidden. The block is static with one
              fixed id, so it has no identity of its own to fall back on.
            {% endcomment %}
            {% content_for 'block',
              type: '_mionas-google-review-card',
              id: 'static-review-card',
              rating: review.rating.value,
              quote: review.comment.value,
              name: review.author.value,
              card_index: rendered_count
            %}
          </div>
          {%- assign rendered_count = rendered_count | plus: 1 -%}
        {%- endif -%}
      {%- endfor -%}
    {%- endcapture -%}

    {%- liquid
      # Create an array from the list items to be used for different layout types
      assign list_items_array = list_items | strip | split: '<!--@list/split-->'
    -%}

    {%- comment -%}
      content_type is documented as 'products' | 'collections' | 'articles' and reviews are none of
      those, but resource-list only reads it in the 'editorial' branch, to choose between three
      position-only wrappers (editorial-product-grid / editorial-blog-grid /
      editorial-collection-grid). All three are content-agnostic -- they place opaque HTML strings
      into grid cells and never look at the item. 'products' is passed because its arrangement suits
      a row of equal-weight cards best; nothing product-specific is emitted.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {% render 'resource-list',
      list_items: list_items,
      list_items_array: list_items_array,
      settings: section.settings,
      carousel_ref: 'mionasGoogleReviewsCarousel',
      slide_count: show_count,
      content_type: 'products',
      test_id: 'mionas-google-reviews-list'
    %}

    {%- comment -%}
      The summary slot: a container block whose children -- score, separator, count, link -- are
      each separately editable. No --horizontal-alignment is set on this wrapper on purpose; the
      container is a group and owns its own direction, alignment and gap.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <div class="section-resource-list__content">
      {%- content_for 'block', type: '_mionas-google-reviews-summary', id: 'static-summary' -%}
    </div>
  </div>
{%- endif -%}

{% stylesheet %}
  /* Layout (display, gaps, padding, width) is owned by the section/section-resource-list/
     spacing-style/gap-style classes, exactly as in product-list; this class is only a scoping
     hook plus the styles unique to this section's own text. */
  .mionas-google-reviews .resource-list__item {
    display: flex;
    height: 100%;
  }

  .mionas-google-reviews .resource-list__item > .review-card {
    width: 100%;
  }
{% endstylesheet %}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Mionas: Google reviews",
  "disabled_on": {
    "groups": ["header", "footer"]
  },
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "@theme"
    },
    {
      "type": "@app"
    },
    {
      "type": "_divider"
    }
  ],
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "review_count",
      "label": "Reviews shown",
      "min": 1,
      "max": 25,
      "step": 1,
      "default": 5,
      "info": "Which reviews appear rotates daily. Clamped to the number of enabled reviews, so asking for more than exist simply shows them all."
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "t:content.layout"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "layout_type",
      "label": "t:settings.layout_type",
      "options": [
        {
          "value": "grid",
          "label": "t:options.grid"
        },
        {
          "value": "carousel",
          "label": "t:options.carousel"
        },
        {
          "value": "editorial",
          "label": "t:options.editorial"
        }
      ],
      "default": "grid"
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "carousel_on_mobile",
      "label": "t:settings.carousel_on_mobile",
      "default": false,
      "visible_if": "{{ section.settings.layout_type != 'carousel' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "columns",
      "label": "t:settings.columns",
      "min": 1,
      "max": 5,
      "step": 1,
      "default": 3,
      "visible_if": "{{ section.settings.layout_type != 'editorial' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "mobile_columns",
      "label": "t:settings.mobile_columns",
      "options": [
        {
          "value": "1",
          "label": "t:options.one_number"
        },
        {
          "value": "2",
          "label": "t:options.two_number"
        }
      ],
      "default": "1",
      "visible_if": "{{ section.settings.layout_type == 'grid' and section.settings.carousel_on_mobile == false }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "mobile_card_size",
      "label": "t:settings.mobile_columns",
      "options": [
        {
          "value": "60cqw",
          "label": "t:options.one_number"
        },
        {
          "value": "44cqw",
          "label": "t:options.two_number"
        }
      ],
      "default": "60cqw",
      "visible_if": "{{ section.settings.layout_type == 'carousel' or section.settings.carousel_on_mobile == true }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "columns_gap",
      "label": "t:settings.horizontal_gap",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 100,
      "step": 1,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 16,
      "visible_if": "{{ section.settings.layout_type == 'grid' or section.settings.layout_type == 'carousel' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "rows_gap",
      "label": "t:settings.vertical_gap",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 100,
      "step": 1,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 16,
      "visible_if": "{{ section.settings.layout_type == 'grid'}}"
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "t:content.carousel_navigation",
      "visible_if": "{{ section.settings.layout_type == 'carousel' or section.settings.carousel_on_mobile == true }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "icons_style",
      "label": "t:settings.icon",
      "options": [
        {
          "value": "arrow",
          "label": "t:options.arrows"
        },
        {
          "value": "chevron",
          "label": "t:options.chevrons"
        },
        {
          "value": "arrows_large",
          "label": "t:options.arrows_large"
        },
        {
          "value": "chevron_large",
          "label": "t:options.chevron_large"
        },
        {
          "value": "none",
          "label": "t:options.none"
        }
      ],
      "default": "arrow",
      "visible_if": "{{ section.settings.layout_type == 'carousel' or section.settings.carousel_on_mobile == true }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "icons_shape",
      "label": "t:settings.icon_background",
      "options": [
        {
          "value": "none",
          "label": "t:options.none"
        },
        {
          "value": "circle",
          "label": "t:options.circle"
        },
        {
          "value": "square",
          "label": "t:options.square"
        }
      ],
      "default": "none",
      "visible_if": "{{ section.settings.icons_style != 'none' and section.settings.layout_type == 'carousel' or section.settings.carousel_on_mobile == true }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "t:content.section_layout"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "section_width",
      "label": "t:settings.width",
      "options": [
        {
          "value": "page-width",
          "label": "t:options.page"
        },
        {
          "value": "full-width",
          "label": "t:options.full"
        }
      ],
      "default": "page-width"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "gap",
      "label": "t:settings.gap",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 100,
      "step": 1,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 24
    },
    {
      "type": "color",
      "id": "background_color",
      "label": "t:settings.background_color",
      "placeholder": "t:settings.default"
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "t:content.padding"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "padding-block-start",
      "label": "t:settings.top",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 100,
      "step": 1,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 48
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "padding-block-end",
      "label": "t:settings.bottom",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 100,
      "step": 1,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 48
    }
  ],
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "Mionas: Google reviews",
      "category": "t:categories.basic",
      "settings": {
        "layout_type": "grid",
        "carousel_on_mobile": false,
        "columns": 3,
        "mobile_columns": "1",
        "mobile_card_size": "60cqw",
        "columns_gap": 16,
        "rows_gap": 16,
        "icons_style": "arrow",
        "icons_shape": "circle",
        "section_width": "page-width",
        "gap": 24,
        "padding-block-start": 48,
        "padding-block-end": 48
      },
      "blocks": {
        "static-review-card": {
          "type": "_mionas-google-review-card",
          "name": "Mionas: Google review",
          "static": true,
          "settings": {
            "show_rating": true,
            "show_author": true,
            "quote_clamp_lines": 5
          }
        },
        "static-summary": {
          "type": "_mionas-google-reviews-summary",
          "name": "Mionas: Reviews summary",
          "static": true,
          "settings": {
            "content_direction": "row",
            "vertical_on_mobile": false,
            "horizontal_alignment": "flex-start",
            "vertical_alignment": "center",
            "align_baseline": false,
            "horizontal_alignment_flex_direction_column": "flex-start",
            "vertical_alignment_flex_direction_column": "center",
            "gap": 8,
            "width": "fill",
            "custom_width": 100,
            "width_mobile": "fill",
            "custom_width_mobile": 100,
            "height": "fit",
            "custom_height": 100,
            "border": "none",
            "border_radius": 0,
            "padding-block-start": 0,
            "padding-block-end": 0,
            "padding-inline-start": 0,
            "padding-inline-end": 0
          },
          "blocks": {
            "score": {
              "type": "_mionas-google-reviews-score",
              "name": "Mionas: Reviews score",
              "settings": {
                "show_star": true,
                "role": "label-lg",
                "variant": "primary"
              }
            },
            "separator": {
              "type": "mionas-text",
              "name": "Mionas: Text",
              "settings": {
                "text": "<p>·</p>",
                "variant": "label",
                "size": "lg",
                "color": "tint",
                "tag": "span"
              }
            },
            "count": {
              "type": "_mionas-google-reviews-count",
              "name": "Mionas: Reviews count",
              "settings": {
                "label": "reseñas en Google",
                "role": "label-lg",
                "variant": "default"
              }
            },
            "link": {
              "type": "mionas-link",
              "name": "Mionas: Link",
              "settings": {
                "label": "Verlas todas",
                "open_in_new_tab": true,
                "variant": "primary",
                "size": "sm"
              }
            }
          },
          "block_order": ["score", "separator", "count", "link"]
        }
      }
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
